# Joining the tailnet.
#
# TS_AUTHKEY is used only on the first boot, when there is no state yet.
# Generate one in the admin console under Settings, Keys. For an image you
# flash more than once, make it reusable and pre-authorised; for a single
# board, a one-off key is fine and can be deleted from this file afterwards.
#
# TS_ROUTES turns the board into a subnet router: the other machines on its
# LAN become reachable from the tailnet without installing anything on them.
# That is what makes an ESPHome device, a printer or a NAS reachable from a
# phone. Routes must also be approved once in the admin console.
#
#   TS_AUTHKEY=tskey-auth-...
#   TS_HOSTNAME=garage
#   TS_ROUTES=192.168.68.0/24
#   TS_EXTRA_ARGS="--accept-dns=false"
#
# --accept-dns=false is worth knowing about: by default a node takes DNS
# settings from the tailnet, which on a headless board is rarely what you
# want and occasionally breaks name resolution it already had.

TS_AUTHKEY=
TS_HOSTNAME=
TS_ROUTES=
TS_EXTRA_ARGS=
